			<div class="content" id="post-content-4835770">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A sentient, living shadow, who belongs to a man named Clarence.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;The&nbsp;Friendly&nbsp;Shadow's&nbsp;Quirk&nbsp;Ideas</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Whether these are a good ideas or not is why I'm putting these here. Yell out if any seem good or bad. I always like to hear feedback and opinions.</p>
<p>The shadow &quot;Tom&quot; can move off of Clarence and interact with other shadows of people and objects. When XXXX interacts with any other shadow, he can interact with it like we could. If he picks up the shadow of a remote, it will float above the spot he is holding it. If he pats someone's shadow on the back, the physical person will feel the same effect. He can do this off and on Clarence.<br />
The shadow can only talk to people through charades. It doesn't have a physical mouth, so it can't talk.<br /></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> It revolves around the wholesome relationship between Clarence and his Shadow.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Expanding&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I'm hoping to let this be emotional. I want a rather wholesome attachment with Clarence and his shadow &quot;Tom&quot;. They have known of each other since childhood. It's not some recent anomaly. They've been best friends or life. Sharing each other accomplishments, laughing together, and working together. Even if Shadow's accomplishments are more private and hidden to onlookers.</p>
<p>The big twist is that the shadow created Clarence.</p>
<p>Tom comes from a world of his own, where everyone is sentient shadows like himself. Their &quot;shadows&quot; are 3d objects like us. When Tom manifested into this world he unintentionally made Clarence. Tom lies to Clarence of his true origin and uses Clarence as his cab and only friend through this strange world.<br /></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Clarence was made by the Shadow. As a friend and a mobile person to keep attached too and see the world.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;The&nbsp;Inspiration</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>For those who are as nerdy as me, the inspiration behind this was three things.</p>
<ol>
<li>The Movie which has yet to (or may never) be released, Me and My Shadow. Note: If you've seen or are about to look up what this is, you'll know this had the biggest impact of the three.</li>
<li>Peter Pan and his shadow</li>
<li>Doctor Who, Season 4, Episode 8, Silence in the Library.</li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Let me know what can be used (if anything can be). Can't wait to hear from you. -Cope</p>
<p>Thanks Blazer, Karpin, and Claygolem. - Cope</p>

