<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Open&nbsp;for&nbsp;crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>It revolves around the wholesome relationship between Clarence and his Shadow.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>You aren't really telling us enough about the relationship between Clarence and the shadow or really anything else in the story besides that for me to recognize this as a central narrative, and you really should. The whole living shadow thing has been done before with <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-017">017</a> and a bunch of others, except this one is friendly and hangs out with someone, what else?? So this &quot;central narrative&quot; just feels like a tease, may as well not even include one. Give us some more of this.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'm unsure if these listed below make the SCP unique on the site, but I hope this is what you meant by Hook or Attention Grabber. Just yell out if you want me to edit this. It's a sentient shadow (Most Shadow related SCPs I've researched have limited sentience or are just furniture) It's unclear on whether Clarence is anomaly, the shadow, or just both.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>No this isn't a Hook or Attention Grabber, should've just put this stuff in the elevator pitch tbh. You already told us it's a sentient shadow..and just because this is a fully sentient shadow doesn't mean it's any more unique or interesting, would the shadow have a personality to make it memorable, what's gonna make anyone wanna care about these two, what do you have in mind that is gonna make someone wanna read an article like this that has a concept that has been done before better and more successfully? I'll touch on the Clarence and shadow possibly being one in the same later.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I was thinking that the shadow could move off of Clarence and interact with other shadows of people and objects. The shadow can talk to Clarence and others telepathically. The shadow can only talk to Clarence</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is stuff you wanna put in the elevator pitch too. Shadow interactions..are the other shadows already sentient and Clarence shadow is just talking to them, is everybody and everything's shadow sentient if that's what you're going for? If not does he somehow make them sentient, is there a radius where shadows just start interacting with Clarence shadow, why or how are the shadows sentient when interacting with Clarence shadow? Clarence shadow uses telepathy to communicate with not just Clarence but with other people? Okay yeah, and-..oh so Clarence shadow actually can't communicate with anybody else but Clarence? Which one is it? Switched up kinda quickly there haha..</p>
<blockquote>
<p>As you probably saw above, I'm hoping to let this be emotional. I want a rather wholesome attachment with Clarence and his shadow. They have known of each other since childhood. It's not some recent anomaly. Below are a few extra ideas which I would like critique for. I was planning on doing one, but decided to keep my options open for the critters who have been doing this much longer then myself. The shadow is a parasite and is detrimental to Charles's health whether either of them know or not. Forces wish for the shadow to leave Clarence and both protest.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>..And some of this one should've gone into the central narrative. I like the idea of a relationship between an anomalous entity and apparently normal humans being formed for life, the thing is though that's been also been done a million times before. Not that you can't do it or that you shouldn't do it, by all means if that's what you're going for then go. It's just that since that's been already explored before multiple times and more effectively, then there'd have to be something to make it it's own to make it feel like it's at least kind of refreshing or different, but that something is lacking, you haven't given anything to make this stand out besides it's basic abilities and it's connection to a random guy. The parasite thing is kinda eh, I mean I guess it could work as a troll from Wondertainment where they make this parasite look like a miracle drug that makes people think they're seeing their shadows move as a side effect for the rest of their lives when in reality they actually are, this just being another case of it. But again eh, nothing really capturing my attention, on the other hand though the separation bit is intriguing, I'd wanna see what a narrative about two lifelong friends being ripped from each other because one isn't normal would look like. If it's done right it could make for a compelling story and a good use of a normally dry idea.</p>
<p>My overall thoughts: Everything you wanna do here has been done before and what ideas you're using to try and make this unique just feel like they're lacking. I'll throw some ideas out for you. Trotting on Clarence Shadow's origin, Clarence not even having to do anything with the shadow, cutting off the other shadows and making Clarence shadow seemingly the only living shadow of this world, without the need for anyone that leaves him without anyone, Clarence shadow getting so lonely that he somehow creates Clarence as a friend he can have for the rest of his life (cool origin story right? eh? eh??). You could also introduce some comedy elements into this like replacing Clarence shadow's only way of communication, being telepathy, with having to do motions and stuff. Basically being a mime, which could introduce some hilarious scenarios and interviews.</p>
</div>
